WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.360
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:02.068
SPEAKER: Welcome to
this episode of Click

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:03.750
to Deploy, a series
where we show you

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:06.360
how easy it is to deploy
solutions from the Google Cloud

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:07.620
Marketplace.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:09.240
In this episode,
we'll be reviewing

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:12.150
how to set up Databricks
via the Cloud Marketplace.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:15.150
Databricks is a cloud-based
data and analytics platform

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:17.130
used for processing
and transforming

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:18.990
massive quantities of data.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:21.060
Databricks can also
be used to explore

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:22.920
the data through
machine learning models

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:25.710
and enable teams to use
one platform to collaborate

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:28.530
on data, analytics,
and AI workloads.

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:31.050
Let's start by searching for
Databricks in the Google Cloud

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:32.250
Marketplace.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:34.170
We'll choose the first solution.

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:35.790
On the solution
page, please make

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:38.820
sure to read through
the overview, pricing,

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:42.840
documentation, and support to
learn more about this solution.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.390
Pricing for this solution
is billed monthly based

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:47.430
on your subscription plan.

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:50.160
Let's click the Subscribe
button to launch this solution.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:51.900
You'll notice the
Pricing Calculator,

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:54.750
which allows you to model your
estimated monthly costs based

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:56.790
on DBU and time frame.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.650
Start by selecting a plan.

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:00.390
We'll choose the default plan.

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:03.000
Next, choose the
correct billing account.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.560
Agree to the
additional terms, which

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.090
are all about
billing and complying

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:07.960
with the license agreement.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:11.230
Finally, click the Subscribe
button to launch the solution.

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:13.500
Now let's move on to the
next step, which is managing

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.060
our subscription on Databricks.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:17.160
You'll need to register
with a Databricks account

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:18.720
to manage this solution.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:22.140
Sign up or log in to
your Databricks account.

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.150
Let's create a
subscription plan.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.190
We'll choose the
standard subscription.

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:28.380
Next, let's choose Workspaces.

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:30.570
Start by creating
a workspace name.

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:33.690
Let's use the name test-101.

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:35.490
Next, we'll choose a region--

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:39.660
let's choose us-west1--
and a Google project ID.

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:42.060
Choose a name that matches
with the project name

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:43.920
where we subscribe
to Databricks.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:47.160
So let's use test-ctd.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:51.000
As you can see, our Databricks
workspace is running.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.505
Finally, let's test the
cluster to see if it's working.

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:00.150
There you have it--

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:02.580
Databricks cluster deployed
with a click of a button.

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:05.070
If you enjoyed this episode,
please subscribe and hit

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:06.403
the Like button below.

00:02:06.403 --> 00:02:08.820
We encourage you to check out
the Google Cloud Marketplace

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:11.200
and deploy this
solution on your own.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:13.220
Thanks for watching.

